\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Proves exact no-transport localization in a diagonal interacting model and an explicit two-level resonance obstruction to naive stability.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
The complete supplied definition, including source qualifications and the dated literature assessment, was reviewed. The calculation below is an elementary restricted attempt motivated by [S2]; it does not claim novelty or a fresh literature-status determination.

\paragraph{Context and investigated scope.} The complete supplied definition, including source qualifications and the dated literature assessment, was reviewed. The calculation below is an elementary restricted attempt motivated by [S2]; it does not claim novelty or a fresh literature-status determination.

\paragraph{An exactly localized interacting benchmark.} On a finite spin chain let $n_i=(I-Z_i)/2$ and
\[
 H=\sum_i h_i n_i+\sum_iJ_i n_in_{i+1},
\]
with arbitrary real coefficients. Every term is diagonal in the occupation basis, so $[H,n_i]=0$ and $n_i(t)=n_i$ for all time. All product occupation states are eigenvectors, including configurations with any prescribed positive limiting density. The interactions $J_i$ can be nonzero, but there is identically no particle transport because each local occupation is separately conserved.

\paragraph{Why perturbative stability is not automatic.} Add a hopping or spin-flip term of strength $\epsilon$. In a two-configuration subspace with diagonal detuning $\Delta$, the matrix $\left(\begin{smallmatrix}0&\epsilon\\\epsilon&\Delta\end{smallmatrix}\right)$ has mixing angle satisfying $\tan(2\theta)=2\epsilon/\Delta$. At $\Delta=0$, arbitrarily small $\epsilon$ produces equal-weight eigenvectors. Therefore a global eigenvector perturbation bound cannot depend only on the operator strength; it must handle small denominators. At positive density the number of competing configurations grows rapidly with volume, so a fixed-particle estimate supplies no uniform control.

\paragraph{Original-target gap.} The diagonal benchmark is an integrable frozen model, not proof of a robust many-body localized phase. It does not determine which spectral, transport or dynamical definition is stable in an infinite system. The first missing step is a volume-uniform treatment of resonant regions under genuinely transport-generating interactions. No universal disorder threshold or stability for all interactions is inferred from the exact commuting example.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Checked all local commutators, positive-density configurations, resonant mixing and distinction between frozen integrability and stable many-body localization. Model self-audit only; no independent human proof checking. Prompts A and B were applied to this canonical record and its qualified source scope. Checked all local commutators, positive-density configurations, resonant mixing and distinction between frozen integrability and stable many-body localization. Retained unresolved status and zero original-target progress; A volume-uniform control of resonances for transport-generating interactions and a precise infinite-density localization criterion are missing.

Coordinator checked the commuting local occupations and resonant two-configuration mixing calculation, without inferring robustness of the frozen model. This additional check was model-assisted, not independent human verification.

\paragraph{Tools, process and contributions.}
Python 3 was used for file preparation and structural checks; no numerical experiment or theorem prover was used. Contribution prompt A was followed by prompt B. GPT-6 Astra with ultra reasoning drafted the research and performed its stated self-audit; any additional coordinator contribution is identified in the verification and audit. A GPT-6-based Codex coordinator assembled the manuscript and checked repository integration; its exact variant and reasoning configuration were not exposed. No human mathematical contribution, independent human proof check or formal proof certification is supplied. Complete derivations and the consulted source references are included here; private reasoning transcripts are not published.

\paragraph{Final status and first remaining gap.}
\textbf{UNRESOLVED}. A volume-uniform control of resonances for transport-generating interactions and a precise infinite-density localization criterion are missing.

